), (2,8), (5,1), and one more pair around (8,3) and (9,3).\n\nThe rule is therefore: wherever a 0 cell has 0 on all four orthogonal sides, paint that whole cross 3. Overlapping crosses just merge. The centre must lie inside the grid, so all four of its neighbours exist.\n\nIn pair 2 the harness calls 0 the background, but the target colour is still 0 and the recolour is still 3. So 0 and 3 are constants across every pair and do not need to be detected from the grid.\n\n**The test input.** The program scans every interior cell. Each centre whose plus is entirely 0 is stamped in 3, one emit per plus. The final grid is then emitted and returned.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    out = g.copy()\n    h, w = g.shape\n    for y in range(1, h - 1):\n        for x in range(1, w - 1):\n            cells = [(y, x), (y-1, x), (y+1, x), (y, x-1), (y, x+1)]\n            if all(g[a, b] == 0 for a, b in cells):\n                for a, b in cells:\n                    out[a, b] = 3\n                emit(out, f\"Plus of 0s centred at ({y},{x}) recoloured to 3.\")\n    emit(out, \"All plus-shaped 0 regions are now 3.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"recolour":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The puzzle can be solved by finding one small shape and recolouring it."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"In pair 2 the harness calls 0 the background, but the target colour is still 0 and the recolour is still 3."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Plus of 0s centred at (9,5) recoloured to 3."}],"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Each centre whose plus is entirely 0 is stamped in 3, one emit per plus."}],"topology":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**The test input.** The program scans every interior cell."}],"layers":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- In pair 1 the eight changed cells are two pluses that overlap, centred at (9,5) and (10,4)."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Overlapping crosses just merge."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"1a1df9da20b17e292dcad984255e425c52ede087b09192fc4451a6b522359b9d","task_sha256":"0bffae3480d0f5e99650229daa8404ea13c9fc4dc5b8ff363f7ca67734243710","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
